      en: ["A center for animal studies in the national park.", "Located on the western half of the Caribbean island of Hispaniola, in the Republic of Haiti.", "Tropical climate with wet and dry seasons; the country lies in the Atlantic hurricane belt (June-November).", "Port-au-Prince, the capital, is Haiti's political, economic and cultural hub.", "Cap-Haïtien on the north coast is the country's second-largest city and a key port.", "More than half of Haiti's territory is mountainous, with the Massif de la Selle range standing out."]
