      en: "A small park for families. Playground. Seating areas. Thus, the site is among the characteristic points of Haiti, the western half of Hispaniola, reflecting the interplay of French colonial heritage, the country's revolutionary history, mountainous terrain, and the cultivation of coffee, mangoes and sugarcane. Located on the western half of the Caribbean island of Hispaniola, in the Republic of Haiti. Tropical climate with wet and dry seasons; the country lies in the Atlantic hurricane belt (June-November). Port-au-Prince, the capital, is Haiti's political, economic and cultural hub."
